# Copy to .env.local for `npm run dev`, or set these in Vercel's project
# settings. Never commit real keys.
#
# A secret key from your problemsapi account page. It stays on the server:
# the deck route copies the stream and makes each deck's pull with it.
PROBLEMS_API_SECRET_KEY=
# A publishable key (POST /publishable_keys/create with the secret key).
# The browser gets it with each deck, to read the deck and check answers.
PROBLEMS_API_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# The decks, as a JSON list on one line. Each names the `ref` POST
# /streams/share answers for a stream that runs a program; the app copies
# that stream into the secret key's account under the deck's slug, so every
# deploy pulls from the same definition and program. `answers` is
# {"kind":"number"} for a typed number, or {"kind":"choice","options":4}
# when the answer is the number of the right option, tapped on a button.
# `typeset` shows the question's LaTeX with KaTeX instead of its words.
# Boards made before there were decks belong to the deck `times-tables`.
FLASHCARD_DECKS=[{"slug":"times-tables","ref":"","title":"Times tables","intro":"Each deck is 12 cards from the times tables up to 12 × 12. Type your answer and the API checks it.","size":12,"cardSeconds":5,"mistakeSeconds":5,"typeset":true,"answers":{"kind":"number"}}]
# Optional: the API's address (default https://api.problemsapi.com).
PROBLEMS_API_URL=
